WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.750
Agent ID adds a small object model.

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.050
The blueprint is the template,
and it holds the credential.

3
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.508
The agent identities created from it hold

4
00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:11.037
permissions but no
credential of their own.

5
00:00:11.037 --> 00:00:14.899
The big consequence is that the
blueprint is a credential boundary.

6
00:00:14.899 --> 00:00:17.830
One credential serves
every agent of that kind,

7
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.413
and one action on the blueprint reaches
all of them, including future ones.

8
00:00:22.413 --> 00:00:27.051
Second, what a blueprint declares
isn't granted until someone consents,

9
00:00:27.051 --> 00:00:29.488
so real access is a sum you have to read.

10
00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:33.113
Third, every agent gets a
human sponsor at creation.

11
00:00:33.113 --> 00:00:35.280
Now, which clouds actually have this?
